  "verified_behaviors": [
    "Actual User create-installation command records an isolated Pi fixture installation; a Codex parent registers a new Pi child whose persisted adapter, installation, config and policy are independent of the parent",
    "Initial child has queued status/epoch0 and no copied Task, Lease, final message, Native Binding or Session. Actual Core Scheduler claim and preparation create its independent binding",
    "The new Pi child is created only with registered target configuration. A custom stable request to that same typed Pi installation preserves custom target and real Pi identity, without claiming arbitrary generic ACP support",
    "A fault at delegation identity insertion occurs after all child rows were written; explicit outer rollback restores Conversation/message/Turn/Run/delegation counts and leaves FK clean",
    "Original exact request replays the same identity while installation is disabled, and never invokes the creation closure; a new factory call rejects that disabled installation before inserting rows",
    "Wrong requested adapter and inconsistent initial target/workspace plans reject without new rows; wire mapping is bijective across all21 built-in targets",
    "All existing Context material, upload, User send/queue/control, causal cancellation and child-end assertions now execute using the explicit production factory rather than copied parent rows",
    "Original identity graph, frozen role, real discovered-runtime freezing, explicit installation command and frozen MCP Manifest recovery owners pass"
  ],
